    "description": "The AES Corporation is a publicly traded power company with utility, generation, and renewable-energy businesses in the United States and international markets. Its customer base includes regulated utility customers, commercial and industrial buyers, and wholesale power-market counterparties. The company operates an asset-heavy model spanning utilities, thermal generation, renewable development, storage, and related energy infrastructure. Public disclosures reviewed here show that AES remained a public company at the time of the latest announced transaction and that its equity was broadly held rather than owned by a single infrastructure sponsor. In March 2026, a consortium led by Global Infrastructure Partners and EQT announced an agreement to acquire AES, with CalPERS and the Qatar Investment Authority also participating in the consortium. AES stated that the transaction is expected to close in late 2026 or early 2027, subject to shareholder approval and regulatory clearances.",
